  "task": "Task: Estimate evapotranspiration from satellite data\nEstimate daily actual evapotranspiration (ETa) and related biophysical variables over a specified study area using the CMRSET model. It integrates multi-source satellite data (MODIS, VIIRS, Landsat, Sentinel-2, MCD43) with climate datasets (precipitation and PET) to simulate ETa, vegetation indices (EVI, GVMI), and surface reflectances. The workflow includes spatiotemporal alignment of climate and optical imagery, preprocessing for sensor-specific corrections, and model execution via the cmrset.run() function. Outputs include an image collection with bands such as 'aet_cmrset', 'ETa', 'evi', 'P', 'PET', and reflectance bands (blue, green, red, NIR, swir), which are used to generate time-series charts of evapotranspiration and environmental drivers over the Calperum site.",
