  "task": "Task: Classify land cover in positive and negative segments\nClassify land cover in segmented regions derived from Landsat surface reflectance imagery using Random Forest classification. It processes four temporal segments (SEG_01 to SEG_04), separates pixels into positive and negative magnitude classes based on band 'b5', applies thresholds on spectral bands (b3, b4, b5) to isolate specific conditions, trains a Random Forest classifier using labeled samples (DF_SGx, BE_SGx, DD_SGx, Reg_SG2), and produces classified raster outputs for each segment. The final output includes multiple classified maps such as 'Segmento_1_Positivo_ClaRF' and exports one of the filtered segmentation results ('SEGM_04_Negat300final') to Google Drive.",
