  "row_idx": 845,
  "task": "Task: Identify vegetation anomaly periods\nAnalyze MODIS NDVI time series from 2000 to 2020 over Argentina to compute a historical baseline of NDVI values and their standard deviation for each 16-day period. It then evaluates the 2020 NDVI data across nine consecutive 16-day intervals, calculates z-score anomalies by comparing current conditions with the historical mean and standard deviation, and classifies areas with significant negative anomalies (below -0.52 standard deviations) as anomalous. These classified anomalies are stacked into a multi-band image and summed to produce a final frequency map showing how many times each pixel experienced anomalous vegetation decline during January–May 2020. The output is a single-band summary raster visualized with a custom color palette and exported to Google Drive.",
