 {
  "row_idx": 1335,
  "task": "Task: Classify land use with Random Forest\nthe workflow performs land use and land cover classification for six cities in Fujian Province (Ningde, Fuzhou, Putian, Quanzhou, Xiamen, Zhangzhou) using Landsat 5 and 7 surface reflectance data from 2012. It computes spectral indices (NDVI, MNDWI, LSWI, RVI), incorporates SRTM-derived elevation and slope, trains a Random Forest classifier on labeled samples, and generates classified maps for each region. Accuracy assessment is performed via confusion matrices and variable importance charts. The final outputs include classified raster maps exported to Google Drive and area counts for specific classes (e.g., Spartina alterniflora, mangroves, Phragmites australis, soil).",
