 {
  "row_idx": 1365,
  "task": "Task: Estimate forest fuel moisture\nEstimate Live Fuel Moisture Content (LFMC) in forested areas using MODIS MOD09A1 surface reflectance data. It computes the Visible Atmospherically Resistant Index (VARI) from red, green, and NIR bands, normalizes it between seasonal min/max extremes (RVARI), and applies an empirical exponential equation to derive LFMC. A fire history mask excludes recently burned areas (within 5 years), and a forest mask based on tree cover (>10% from Hansen dataset) restricts output to woody vegetation. Monthly composites (2005–2020) are generated, and for each month (Jan, Feb, Aug–Dec), pixel-wise maximum, minimum, and 10th/30th/70th/90th percentiles of LFMC are exported as rasters clipped to the East_Bioreg region.",
